#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293225 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Definite Integral Using Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b176a504-ffd4-5abf-9500-adc45cebbe4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b176a504-ffd4-5abf-9500-adc45cebbe4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293227} :answer-field/id #uuid "70ea796f-ca89-51c5-bda1-3399890e3624" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293226}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0a8a022e-93cb-5904-a68b-7a101ae4d8a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-349231" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=4x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=4 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x) & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 4x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x & =4x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x))-\\int (-\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x))\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{4}{\\pi }x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{4}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{\\pi }x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{4}{{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{\\pi }(1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1)-0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 0))+\\frac{4}{{\\pi }^{2}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{\\pi }(-1-0)+\\frac{4}{{\\pi }^{2}}(0-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293249 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b762e911-a67a-574c-a4a8-ff7f8fdaff2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293251} {:answer/id #uuid "e72f1a55-45cf-514d-aa1d-9182a513cc9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293252} {:answer/id #uuid "5a01268a-495f-57cb-98f4-0a27a629c636" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293253} {:answer/id #uuid "cc55f34e-c81e-5802-aa0c-b307d58e313a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{6}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293254} {:answer/id #uuid "ec3ca75b-8c77-5ed9-879e-4d77dfb6699b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b762e911-a67a-574c-a4a8-ff7f8fdaff2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293251} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3e1e112-a082-54a8-a0bb-62e948227dbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293250}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "53c9558d-d595-5806-b976-b416dcd019a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-74088" :question/problem "$\\int (6x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (6x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x+1\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (6x+1)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(6x+1)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (6x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-6\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
